I'm not.

00:06:59.879 --> 00:07:01.619
I'm not.

00:07:01.619 --> 00:07:04.079
I was a little laundry impaired this morning.

00:07:04.079 --> 00:07:06.000
How bohemian of you.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:06.500
Hey.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:08.659
Do you want to cover the gymnastics tryouts?

00:07:08.659 --> 00:07:09.119
Oh.

00:07:09.119 --> 00:07:09.619
I'm sorry.

00:07:09.619 --> 00:07:11.339
Can you find someone else?

00:07:11.339 --> 00:07:13.799
Pete Ross passing up the opportunity to ogle Smallville

00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:15.259
High's women in spandex?

00:07:15.259 --> 00:07:17.379
Look, I just can't do it, OK?

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:21.139
I got to get to class.

00:07:21.139 --> 00:07:23.259
Well, hang on a second, and I'll walk with you.

00:07:27.759 --> 00:07:29.000
Or not.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:38.740
What?

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.139
Dad, I came as soon as I heard.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.699
Lex, I...

00:07:42.699 --> 00:07:43.319
Are you all right?

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:43.660
Yeah.

00:07:44.199 --> 00:07:46.279
Would you, uh, excuse us, please?

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:47.360
Yeah, I'm fine, son.

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:50.879
I just, uh, bruised a few ribs.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:51.600
That's all.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.519
There are rumors floating around

00:07:54.519 --> 00:07:56.060
that the person who attacked you

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:58.699
was holding an ancient Kowachi artifact

00:07:58.699 --> 00:08:01.860
that supposedly gave him superhuman strength and speed.

00:08:02.099 --> 00:08:02.500
Oh.

00:08:03.879 --> 00:08:06.279
Well, if that were true, wouldn't that be a prize?

00:08:09.959 --> 00:08:11.060
Is that why you've come?

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.719
I don't live in the past anymore, Dad.

00:08:16.399 --> 00:08:17.560
Someone told me it was a weakness.

00:08:19.219 --> 00:08:21.300
Given your recent mishaps in the cave,

00:08:21.399 --> 00:08:23.060
maybe you should start following your own advice.

00:08:26.759 --> 00:08:27.240
Dad.

00:08:28.699 --> 00:08:31.159
Why don't you let me use some of my law enforcement relationships

00:08:31.159 --> 00:08:32.399
to track this guy down?

00:08:33.819 --> 00:08:36.159
Considering what you and I have been going through recently,

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:37.700
this...

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.700
filial concern of yours is...

00:08:41.559 --> 00:08:43.980
is touching and a little surprising.

00:08:46.019 --> 00:08:47.120
Who are you, Lex?

00:08:50.899 --> 00:08:51.379
Dad.

00:08:52.799 --> 00:08:54.679
No matter what our difference is,

00:08:55.779 --> 00:08:58.340
I'm always gonna be concerned about your well-being.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.400
I'm not gonna be concerned about you.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:01.259
I'm gonna be concerned about you.

00:09:01.259 --> 00:09:02.160
I'm not gonna be concerned about you.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:02.600
I'm not gonna be concerned about you.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.500
You know, Lex, the only thing more bruised in my ribs is my ego.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.860
Any more publicity would only embarrass me.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.720
So, the cave.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:13.400
What do you say?

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:14.640
Let's let the matter drop.

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:15.500
All right?

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:15.560
All right.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.860
You didn't get in?

00:09:31.759 --> 00:09:32.180
No.

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:34.000
No, I got accepted.

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.940
They turned down my financial aid,

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:40.580
which means I can't go.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.580
Well, wait a minute.

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:52.720
Before you commit yourself to pouring lattes in the sunflower state,

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.379
why don't you talk to Lex?

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.040
Chloe, I'm not asking Lex for a loan.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:58.680
Why not?

00:09:58.679 --> 00:09:58.939
Why not?

00:09:59.019 --> 00:10:00.699
You know he would happily lend it to you.

00:10:00.899 --> 00:10:02.459
But I wanted to do this on my own.

00:10:03.979 --> 00:10:06.799
Well, selfishly, I would be glad if you decided to stay.

00:10:08.059 --> 00:10:09.579
But if Lex were in your shoes,

00:10:09.659 --> 00:10:12.099
do you honestly think that he would let one bump in the road

00:10:12.099 --> 00:10:13.639
deter him from pursuing his dreams?

00:10:15.299 --> 00:10:16.019
Call him.

00:10:28.679 --> 00:10:43.179
Here for the prospective students tour club?

00:10:44.059 --> 00:10:45.039
Did you do this?

00:10:46.019 --> 00:10:48.199
What possible reason would I have

00:10:48.199 --> 00:10:50.899
to ransack the office of an obscure teaching assistant?

00:10:51.599 --> 00:10:52.740
Then tell me why you're here.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:54.379
You first.

00:10:55.579 --> 00:10:56.299
I'm coming.

00:10:57.859 --> 00:10:58.019
Jeremiah,

00:10:58.019 --> 00:11:00.019
Jeremiah was gonna help me with a term paper.

00:11:02.019 --> 00:11:04.019
Term paper.

00:11:06.019 --> 00:11:10.019
So your visit doesn't have anything to do with the fact that he went ballistic in the caves last night

00:11:10.019 --> 00:11:12.019
and absconded with a sacred Quachi artifact?

00:11:14.019 --> 00:11:16.019
I didn't know.

00:11:18.019 --> 00:11:20.019
Well, I'm surprised.

00:11:20.019 --> 00:11:24.019
I mean, you usually keep such a close eye on everything that happens in the caves.

00:11:24.019 --> 00:11:26.019
But those term papers, you're always writing.

00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:28.019
You still haven't told me why you're here.

00:11:30.019 --> 00:11:32.019
Well, according to the legend of Neman and Sagith,

00:11:32.019 --> 00:11:36.019
this missing artifact bestows extraordinary abilities on whoever possesses it.

00:11:36.019 --> 00:11:38.019
You don't really believe that.

00:11:38.019 --> 00:11:41.019
I like to keep my mind open to extreme possibilities.

00:11:46.019 --> 00:11:48.019
You're starting to sound like your father.

00:11:51.019 --> 00:11:53.019
I guess I should be offended, but, uh...

00:11:56.019 --> 00:11:58.019
It looks like he's beaten us both to the punch.

00:12:08.019 --> 00:12:10.019
Tell me something, Clark.

00:12:14.019 --> 00:12:16.019
Do you have any idea what this might be?

00:12:21.019 --> 00:12:23.019
Oh.

00:12:23.019 --> 00:12:25.019
If you find your friend, tell him I'd like to meet him.

00:12:26.019 --> 00:12:28.019
And good luck with your term paper.

00:12:38.019 --> 00:12:41.019
Even if I knew where he was, what makes you think he'd listen to me?

00:12:41.019 --> 00:12:45.019
But as I understand it, you're not only his academic advisor,

00:12:45.019 --> 00:12:47.019
but you're his, uh...

00:12:47.019 --> 00:12:51.019
spiritual counselor as well, yes?

00:12:51.019 --> 00:12:55.019
So why not just explain to him that the Starblade isn't his to keep?

00:12:55.019 --> 00:12:57.019
What do you know about it?

00:12:57.019 --> 00:12:59.019
I've read your writings, Professor.

00:12:59.019 --> 00:13:02.019
Well, it doesn't belong to you either.

00:13:02.019 --> 00:13:05.019
You know I have a considerable amount of influence around here.

00:13:05.019 --> 00:13:06.019
Yes?

00:13:06.019 --> 00:13:07.019
It's not a threat.

00:13:07.019 --> 00:13:09.019
No. Of course not.

00:13:09.019 --> 00:13:11.019
But I'm fascinated by your work.

00:13:11.019 --> 00:13:15.019
I'm thinking about giving your department a sizable grant

00:13:15.019 --> 00:13:17.019
so you can continue your research.

00:13:19.019 --> 00:13:23.019
Don't tell me an educated man like you puts stock in old Indian legends.

00:13:23.019 --> 00:13:24.019
Look, Professor.

00:13:25.019 --> 00:13:28.019
You and I both saw what Jeremiah did in the cave.

00:13:31.019 --> 00:13:35.019
I've suspected for some time that there are special human beings

00:13:35.019 --> 00:13:37.019
who are capable of feats like that.

00:13:37.019 --> 00:13:39.019
Now I know I'm right.

00:13:39.019 --> 00:13:41.019
If you've read my work,

00:13:41.019 --> 00:13:45.019
then you also know that the blade will crumble if the wrong person touches it.

00:13:45.019 --> 00:13:47.019
Yes.

00:13:49.019 --> 00:13:51.019
Sageeth.

00:13:51.019 --> 00:13:54.019
Who is he?

00:13:54.019 --> 00:13:59.019
According to legend, he's the Bearer of Darkness.

00:14:02.019 --> 00:14:03.019
Clark.

00:14:03.019 --> 00:14:06.019
Well, this is a coincidence.

00:14:06.019 --> 00:14:08.019
It's nice to see you.

00:14:11.019 --> 00:14:12.019
Professor.

00:14:15.019 --> 00:14:16.019
What did he want?

00:14:17.019 --> 00:14:19.019
Same thing you do, Naman.

00:14:19.019 --> 00:14:21.019
Professor, please stop talking.

00:14:21.019 --> 00:14:22.019
Stop calling me that.

00:14:22.019 --> 00:14:28.019
One who denies his destiny can bring about as much pain and suffering as your greatest enemy.

00:14:28.019 --> 00:14:30.019
Please, Professor. I'm just here to help.

00:14:32.019 --> 00:14:35.019
I don't want Jeremiah to hurt anyone, including himself.

00:14:36.019 --> 00:14:39.019
This mural was painted on the blinds in his office.

00:14:39.019 --> 00:14:40.019
I tried drawing it.

00:14:45.019 --> 00:14:47.019
Clark. That's a slumbery place.

00:14:47.019 --> 00:14:55.019
A burial ground where the ancient Kwajtch used to perform death rituals.

00:14:55.019 --> 00:14:58.019
Jeremiah is writing his dissertation about it.

00:14:58.019 --> 00:15:00.019
Does it still exist?

00:15:00.019 --> 00:15:03.019
Yes.

00:15:10.019 --> 00:15:12.519
Now imperfection.

00:15:12.519 --> 00:15:21.120
Jeremiah!

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:21.360
